---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Hardware Testing Methodology"
  description="How The Silicon Ledger tests processors, GPUs, laptops, and memory subsystems using independent power-rail telemetry and zero manufacturer sponsorships."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl rounded-2xl border border-stone-300 bg-[#FCFBF8] p-8 shadow-sm">
    <div class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#D9381E]">
      Masthead &amp; Lab Methodology
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-extrabold text-[#141413]">
      Independent Silicon Testing &amp; Buyer Advocacy
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-stone mt-6 max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:font-bold prose-p:text-[#141413]">
      <p>
        <strong>The Silicon Ledger</strong> is an independent hardware testing laboratory and buyer-advocacy publication dedicated to uncovering how consumer laptops, mobile SoCs, and graphics processors actually perform after the keynote applause fades.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Testing Methodology</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Sustained Thermal Loops (30-Minute Minimum):</strong> Rather than citing single-pass burst scores that favour undersized cooling assemblies, every laptop and smartphone is tested over a 30-minute continuous loop in a climate-controlled 22°C chamber.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Inline Power-Rail Telemetry:</strong> We measure board and package power draw directly across the DC-in and PMIC rails to quantify performance-per-watt curves.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Secondary Market Value Indexing:</strong> New hardware is never evaluated in a vacuum. Every review compares launch MSRP against current verified street prices of prior-generation flagships.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Editorial Independence &amp; Monetization Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Manufacturers never preview our scores, teardown findings, or headlines prior to publication. The Silicon Ledger is funded through programmatic display advertising and reader-supported retail affiliate links. When you purchase hardware through links on our site, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
